CORE
a.c
b.c --backward-impact
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
\*\* helper \*\*
^-.*function helper
^\+.*function helper
--
^warning: ignoring
^D.*function helper
//
// --backward-impact propagates impact backward from the change. On these
// inputs it emits the syntactic-diff markers (-/+) but, unlike
// --forward-impact / --change-impact, no forward data-dependence (D) line --
// asserted here as a disallowed pattern so the test distinguishes the modes.
